1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:03,470
Why is the sky blue? Why
not purple, or white?

2
00:00:03,570 --> 00:00:07,170
Good question. The answer is
hiding inside sunlight.

3
00:00:12,020 --> 00:00:15,790
Sunlight looks white, but it is really
every colour mixed together.

4
00:00:15,890 --> 00:00:20,710
Each colour travels as a wave. Red waves
are long. Blue waves are short.

5
00:00:21,360 --> 00:00:23,090
When sunlight hits the air,

6
00:00:23,130 --> 00:00:27,390
tiny gas molecules bounce the short blue
waves all over the sky.

7
00:00:27,490 --> 00:00:30,880
Blue light scatters almost six
times more than red light.

8
00:00:31,530 --> 00:00:35,213
Violet scatters even more. But
the sun sends less violet,

9
00:00:35,253 --> 00:00:37,800
and our eyes are less sensitive to it.

10
00:00:38,450 --> 00:00:43,540
So the sky is blue because the air
scatters blue sunlight in every direction.

11
00:00:44,190 --> 00:00:46,340
Then why are sunsets orange?

12
00:00:46,440 --> 00:00:48,400
That is our next question!

